{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Secuura/Distributed_Secuura/pulls/2227","id":5288402895,"node_id":"PR_kwDORcHGMc8AAAABOzafzw","html_url":"https://github.com/Secuura/Distributed_Secuura/pull/2227","diff_url":"https://github.com/Secuura/Distributed_Secuura/pull/2227.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/Secuura/Distributed_Secuura/pull/2227.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Secuura/Distributed_Secuura/issues/2227","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Secuura/Distributed_Secuura/pulls/2227/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Secuura/Distributed_Secuura/pulls/2227/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Secuura/Distributed_Secuura/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Secuura/Distributed_Secuura/issues/2227/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Secuura/Distributed_Secuura/statuses/e29f8e8fa4b6ff15ffb3c749d400b93586f66aab","number":2227,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Refs KS-2195: refresh hono 4.13.13 -> 4.13.18 in the root and mcp-server locks","user":{"login":"kksecura","id":258699643,"node_id":"U_kgDOD2txew","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/258699643?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kksecura","html_url":"https://github.com/kksecura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kksecura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kksecura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kksecura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kksecura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kksecura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kksecura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kksecura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kksecura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kksecura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Refs KS-2195\n\n**BLUF.** After PR 2226 (KS-2194) merged, the pre-push legs 6 and 7 still refused every push, now on `hono` 4.13.13 (3 new advisories). This PR is an in-range, lock-only refresh of `hono` 4.13.13 -> 4.13.18 in the two locks that carry it: two files, 3 lines each. No manifest edit, no baseline row. It clears GHSA-4m76-xfj5-7975, GHSA-h7mg-cq63-vhpq and GHSA-3gg2-335m-rxc6 (listed by npm's feed) and GHSA-46wx-v44x-9hh2 and GHSA-4h7h-rv7c-7m2v (listed by GitHub, not yet in npm's feed).\n\nBefore this deploys: nothing deploys from this PR; deploy is Kam's tap.\n\n## Test Evidence\n\nHost Node v26.8.1, npm 11.19.0 (NOT Node 24). Base `a288aa45d6b2` (develop after PR 2226), head `e29f8e8fa4b6`. Every run is in a throwaway clone after `npm ci --ignore-scripts`, output to files, rc recorded.\n\n**Touched:** `Blockchain/Dev/package-lock.json` and `Blockchain/Dev/services/mcp-server/package-lock.json`, only `version`, `resolved` and `integrity` of `node_modules/hono` (`git diff --numstat` 3 3 each; no libc, os or cpu line moved). Both `package.json` files and `scripts/audit/audit-baseline.json` are byte-identical (sha256 before = after; baseline `d6e7f1ed1175...`).\n\n**Ran:**\n- Legs 6 and 7 BEFORE (base): `audit:gate` rc 1, \"8 distinct advisories reported, 5 baselined\", 3 NEW; `audit:locks` rc 1, \"45 standalone lockfiles\", \"7 advisories match, 4 already baselined\", the same 3 NEW in `services/mcp-server`.\n- Legs 6 and 7 AFTER (head): `audit:gate` rc 0, \"5 distinct advisories reported, 5 baselined\", OK; `audit:locks` rc 0, \"45 standalone lockfiles\", \"4 advisories match, 4 already baselined\", OK. All five hono ids and both node-server ids occur 0 times in either AFTER output, and there is no FAIL section. GHSA-46wx-v44x-9hh2 and GHSA-4h7h-rv7c-7m2v occurred 0 times BEFORE too (npm's feed does not list them yet), so for those two the proof is the range, not an audit-output absence: GitHub `/advisories` gives `< 4.13.16` and `>= 4.5.1, <= 4.13.15`, first patched 4.13.16, and 4.13.18 is outside both.\n- The hook's own legs 6 and 7 on the pushed branch: both OK, same figures (\"5 distinct advisories reported, 5 baselined\"; \"45 standalone lockfiles\").\n- `audit:contract` rc 0: tests 62, pass 62, fail 0, skipped 0.\n- Advisory ranges: GitHub `/advisories?affects=hono&ecosystem=npm` (61 rows; range evaluator with a planted control): 5 ranges include 4.13.13, 0 include 4.13.18. npm `dist-tags.latest` is 4.13.18; npm's bulk advisory feed for `hono` 4.13.18 returns `[]`. Re-read at the push: develop unchanged at `a288aa45d6b2`, 0 new hono ids.\n- Census (JSON parse of all 47 tracked `package-lock.json`, four planted controls OK): BEFORE 2 locks at `hono` 4.13.13; AFTER 2 at 4.13.18 and 45 with none; `@hono/node-server` 2.1.8 in both. `merge-base --is-ancestor a288aa45d6b2 <head>` rc 0.\n- Root `npm ci --ignore-scripts` rc 0 BEFORE and AFTER (1794 packages). `npm ls hono @hono/node-server --package-lock-only --all` rc 0: ONE copy of `hono` 4.13.18 under the SDK 1.32.1, `@prisma/dev` 0.24.3 and the node-server peer; no 4.13.13 anywhere.\n- mcp-server whole suite on the Dockerfile route (isolated copy, standalone-lock `npm ci`, `@secuura/shared` linked from a `packages/shared` built by its own `npm ci` and build): BEFORE and AFTER both 15 of 15 files, 137 of 137 tests, rc 0; `tsc` (`npm run build -- --noEmit`) rc 0 both. The suite is a no-regression check, not a `hono`-path check, because `hono` is installed but not loaded by mcp-server's two entries (next bullet).\n- Import walk (`module.register` resolve hook over the BUILT dist, 5 s cap, ESM graph only), identical BEFORE and AFTER: `dist/http-server.js` (the Dockerfile CMD) 55 modules resolved, `hono` 0, `@hono/node-server` 0; `dist/index.js` 185, 0, 0; control, the SDK's `server/streamableHttp.js`, 109, 1, 2. Static grep: 0 imports of `hono` or `@hono/*` in mcp-server `dist` and `src` (control: the `express` import is found in 1 dist file).\n- Pre-push hook on the pushed branch, verbatim: `PREFLIGHT INCOMPLETE — 13/16 legs ran, 3 SKIPPED. Nothing failed.` Legs 3, 4 and 8 were skipped (\"local stack not up on http://localhost:6882\"). This is not a pass of those legs.\n- Dry run of the refresh verb in a throwaway `git archive` of the base: the same three lines and the same integrity.\n\n**NOT run / NOT covered:** no runtime exercise of the MCP server against a live HTTP client (its HTTP entry was only started for the 5 s import walk); no image build; no deploy; the hook's legs 3, 4 and 8, and Schemathesis, Akto, Playwright and k6, were not run (their acknowledgment boxes stay unticked); `services/originate` is unchanged; the `hono` 4.13.13 -> 4.13.18 code diff was not read; CommonJS `require` paths, `@prisma/dev` reachability and every other shipped entry are not measured; npm's advisory feed does not yet list GHSA-46wx-v44x-9hh2 and GHSA-4h7h-rv7c-7m2v.\n\n**Migrations and config:** none.\n\n**Docs:** no fragment pair. `.claude/skills/secuura-test-discipline/SKILL.md` lines 483-484 say \"If a change genuinely does not affect either doc, say so explicitly and why\". This PR adds no test, probe or gate and changes no documented behaviour; it moves one dependency's version, resolved URL and integrity in two lock files.\n\nSibling: KS-2194 (`@hono/node-server`, PR 2226) is untouched. A tier 1 gate is requested: a wrong lock re-freezes every push.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-13T01:38:06Z","updated_at":"2026-11-13T01:38:13Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"f8548f375c353379f62f7a94f917498219b0905e","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"Secuura:feature/ks-2195-hono-advisories-on-hono-41313-ghsa-4m76-xfj5","ref":"feature/ks-2195-hono-advisories-on-hono-41313-ghsa-4m76-xfj5","repo":{"id":1170327089,"node_id":"R_kgD